      {
        "id": 219254,
        "name": "Hankroyd",
        "username": "Hankroyd",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/cc9497/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-06-15T21:39:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Well, when you are immortal you get used to see other as fireworks.</p><p>But it's the same with every death : Life goes on.</p><p>People die everyday, but other people are born too.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>When you are mortal, you see your elder die, then as you grow older, you see the next generations inherating of your world.</p><p>But when you are immortal, you see older people dying, your friend getting older and dying too, their child getting older and dying too ... and so on. Some immortals can't take it and usually find a remote location to live without dealing with it. Otherwise, if the immortals manage to find a way to cope with it, he can live his eternal life more or less normally.</p><p>Mr Frost is unusual by the fact he need a suit to live, he can't blend easily in the human society. And he is too young to already having to deal with the 'immortal crisis' (usually happens between 50 to 60 yo). So ... No sure how his armor will be a help or a hindrance to pass this stage. Time wil tell ... :)</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:51:32.225Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
