      {
        "id": 219255,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-06-15T22:00:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Being with the Sentinels of Freedom will help.&nbsp; Sure, the former F5 will eventually die off, but there will be new teams with new heroes who he'll help mentor.</p><p>I don't think it would ever come to this, though.&nbsp; Remember how Felicity is the first Legacy to become a full-fledged hero while the previous Parsons was still alive?&nbsp; That holds true for other superheroes as well.&nbsp; AZ is at least as likely to die by violence as any of them.<span>&nbsp; He may be immortal, but he's also incredibly fragile.&nbsp; His suit breaks all the damn time.&nbsp; The chances of him still being alive when everyone he cares about is dead are pretty slim.</span></p><p><span>I don't think he'd outright commit suicide even then, though.&nbsp; He'd probably just have a death wish when it comes to taking on more and more dangerous missions with worse and worse odds of survival.</span></p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:51:32.305Z",
