        "raw": "<p>Being with the Sentinels of Freedom will help.&nbsp; Sure, the former F5 will eventually die off, but there will be new teams with new heroes who he&#39;ll help mentor.</p><p>I don&#39;t think it would ever come to this, though.&nbsp; Remember how Felicity is the first Legacy to become a full-fledged hero while the previous Parsons was still alive?&nbsp; That holds true for other superheroes as well.&nbsp; AZ is at least as likely to die by violence as any of them.<span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp; He may be immortal, but he&#39;s also incredibly fragile.&nbsp; His suit breaks all the damn time.&nbsp; The chances of him still being alive when everyone he cares about is dead are pretty slim.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">I don&#39;t think he&#39;d outright commit suicide even then, though.&nbsp; He&#39;d probably just have a death wish when it comes to taking on more and more dangerous missions with worse and worse odds of survival.</span></p>",
